                <pb facs="0136" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2131/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-25T19:00:00-05:00">September 25, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 26—8:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. My telegram No. 74, September 24, 9 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    informs me that he believes there is no possibility of the adjournment of
                    Congress before the end of the calendar year.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
